<article class="env-lemma" id="06UG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06UG">Lemma <span data-tag="06UG">101.23.8</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y} \to \mathcal{Z}$ be morphisms of algebraic stacks. Assume that $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Z}$ is locally quasi-finite and $\mathcal{Y} \to \mathcal{Z}$ is quasi-DM. Then $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ is locally quasi-finite. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Write $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ as the composition 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{X} \longrightarrow \mathcal{X} \times _\mathcal {Z} \mathcal{Y} \longrightarrow \mathcal{Y}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       The second arrow is locally quasi-finite as a base change of $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Z}$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/06UB" data-tag="06UB">101.23.3</a>. The first arrow is locally quasi-finite by Lemma <a href="/tag/050I" data-tag="050I">101.4.8</a> as $\mathcal{Y} \to \mathcal{Z}$ is quasi-DM. Hence $\mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ is locally quasi-finite by Lemma <a href="/tag/06UD" data-tag="06UD">101.23.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>